{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e","id":1209014,"title":"Anshega April - Cult of Bones 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T14:40:09-07:00","id":1209014,"title":"Anshega April - Cult of Bones 2e","content":"So, because I am incredibly busy at the moment (don't worry, the Tools of Hatred write-up will be coming!), and because I'm on the team for Shunned By The Moon and therefore keeping my best new Anshega material for that forthcoming product, I'm not going to be able to do more than one Anshega April poll this month. However, that doesn't mean I don't have new Anshega April material to share! Here's a 2nd ed update for the Cult of Bones, a Pure Lodge for those of you who want to feature Ivory Claw Belloc or Fire-Touched gravediggers in your chronicles, as requested by one of my patrons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#052D49\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>The Cult of Bones</b></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#052D49\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Gravediggers, Archaeomachs, Ghuls</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">If the past is another country, the Cult of Bones want it to conquer the present. The zealous Pure who make up the Cult\u2019s ranks have a grand goal in mind for their Lodge \u2013 the direct resurrection of the Great Predator itself. This isn\u2019t a hypothetical or metaphorical plan, but an overarching purpose that drives everything the Cult of Bones does. The Gravediggers plan to gather up the earthly remains of the deity and, from its bones, build it anew. Then, as the Cult sees it, the Wolf will again walk the world, all wrongs will be set right, and the Pure shall rule over the paradise of Pangaea once more, subjugating all that exists and turning all of creation to the purpose of honouring their progenitor each passing day and night.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">What makes the Cult of Bones\u2019 plan different to the wild schemes of the mad-eyed deluded is that it approaches this ultimate goal systematically, and has made considerable strides already. Whatever the metaphysical state that befell the Great Predator when it died, there do seem to have been tangible fragments left over \u2013 gobbets of divine substance that retain traces of the Wolf\u2019s power. Cultists travel the world, seeking out major hotspots of Uratha history in search for these shattered shards of the Great Predator, reaching out to local Pure for aid in digging up the past in return for favours, fetishes, and influence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Cult\u2019s efforts go beyond digging up the dead pieces of Wolf; they\u2019ve come into a number of other ancient carcasses and fragments over the years, including what may be truly dead Shards of the Spinner Hag, a massive mouldering colossus buried under Sudan, and what seems to have been a ritually mummified leviathan of the Void Beyond \u2013 a metaphysically-preserved nightmare, though who mummified it, how, and why, is still unknown. Some assume that it is these dead ancients that are the Cult\u2019s prey, and that is true in a manner of speaking, but the actual prey to whom the Cult have refined their hunt is all the more worrying. Gravediggers hunt wolf spirits and Uratha ancestor spirits, not to draw upon their wisdom but to literally drain them of power or bind them. If Mother Wolf was weakened before its death, then the Cult must restore that strength, and so they hunt for those spirits with the closest resonance to the Great Predator. Cult ritualists bind the hunted spirits for Essence extraction, feeding their power into the relics that the Lodge has managed to gather, or imprison them in fetishes to further serve the Cult. A few are forcibly bound to work directly for the Gravediggers as attack spirits, trackers, and bone-hunters.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Gravediggers are not a hidden cult; they are widely known of amongst the Pure, and they have leveraged their considerable membership, the respect for their goal, and their network of resources into significant power as a result. The Cult doesn\u2019t take just anyone, leaning towards the more cerebral and zealous; it wouldn\u2019t be accurate to just categorise them as occult archaeologists, but the Cult of Bones does hold a significant number of scholars. Other Pure fear the Cult of Bones because the Gravediggers believe their goal justifies the means, any means, and they are more than happy to sacrifice lesser Pure to take another step up that ladder towards Wolf\u2019s revival. Worse, the Cult\u2019s treatment of spirits is at odds with the Pure\u2019s reverence for the mighty totems that oversee the global war against the Forsaken, and that scares many Anshega. The Cult focuses its predations on wolf and ancestor spirits that serve the Forsaken, but they are not above picking off the spiritual allies of Pure who do not co-operate with the Lodge\u2019s agenda.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Totem: Father\u2019s Howl</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Cult of Bones holds that Father\u2019s Howl is literally the echoing, final howl of Father Wolf \u2013 a death-scream given sentience and the driving will to mastermind its creator\u2019s will. This is both true and false; Father\u2019s Howl is an ancient spirit of death that was born from the tumult of the Great Predator\u2019s demise, but it does not have any more of a divine link to the Great Predator than any spirit does to the circumstances of its creation. Nonetheless, Father\u2019s Howl is a very powerful spirit, close to vying the might of the Firstborn themselves, and it is this spiritual strength that gives the Cult of Bones the leeway they need to pursue their schemes without the meddling of the other Pure totems.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Father\u2019s Howl appears as a presence, rather than a physical mass; the air ripples with a constant, wailing echo, as if a thousand wolves were distantly howling. The Howl can extend its presence to wash over a whole city block, or fold its scream down into the palm of a werewolf\u2019s cupped hand; it also has the ability to Fetter itself to an Uratha\u2019s breath, hiding in the stream and pulse of their lungs and voice. When it lets itself loose, stone shatters and buildings topple. It is sometimes mistaken for a storm or wind spirit, but it is very much a spirit of death; where it passes, weak lives are snuffed out, and ghosts shiver and dance in frenzied agitation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Father\u2019s Howl has a simple agenda, one that entirely matches with its followers; the return of Father Wolf to the world. It believes that when this happens, the Great Predator will embrace it as a favoured child and inheritor. Howl bears a burning hatred for Luna; in the aftermath of the Sundering, it called to the Moon to recognise it as the successor to Wolf, born of Wolf\u2019s death and last howl as it was. Luna refused to acknowledge it, and denied it the Warden Moon\u2019s favour and the mark of legitimacy the god could have bestowed upon it \u2013 not a metaphorical notion but a very real crowning with power that Howl believes would have rallied the Firstborn under its reign. By denying this, Luna instigated the strife and war that would follow, and so Father\u2019s Howl holds the mad god responsible not just for the rejection of its own ascension, but for all the carnage among the Uratha that has followed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Howl\u2019s relationship with the Firstborn has long been troubled; it claims to have aided the Pure Firstborn during the early formation of the Tribes, but while there is certainly obligation from the three great wolves to Father\u2019s Howl, they also seem to resent its claims to greatness and its hunger for power. Howl has gathered many spirits to its court and established itself as a major pillar within Pure society, strong enough to be independent from the totems that flock to the Firstborns\u2019 skirts, but it yet remains denied the respect and rule it feels it is due. Often, it takes out its frustration on Lunes that it manages to catch or that the Cult brings to it, brutally torturing them for its own amusement. Sometimes, it intentionally sends its Cult to target the ancestor spirits or wolf spirit allies of the Pure Tribes in order to steal away some of the Firstborns\u2019 strength and assert its own power against them.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bonds</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Blessing:</i> When resisting or contesting a rite that a Lodge member is conducting, spirits suffer a penalty equal to the dots in the highest Influence they possess that is either Influence (Wolves) or an Influence directly to Uratha, such as that which an ancestor spirit may possess. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Aspiration:</i> To retrieve remains that have been buried or hidden. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Ban: </i>A Lodge member cannot display humbleness about their own accomplishments. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sacred Hunt </b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Lodge Sacred Hun grants your character the ability to tear the Essence from certain spirit-prey. Against spirits that have Influence (Wolves) or an Influence directly relating to Uratha, your character is able to strike these ephemeral entities with their natural weaponry, and any such hit also drains a single point of Essence from the victim. This Essence is not destroyed; it is drained away into the Cult\u2019s eldritch vaults where ancient god-fragments lie slumbering.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Secrets of the Gravediggers</b></span></span></span></span></div><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Cult of Bones have tried ritual sacrifice of Uratha and Wolf-Blooded to empower the dead bones of Wolf, but with little success. Recently, however, several Gravedigger scholars have begun experimenting with burying victims alive or using other funerary-rites as execution tools; the experiments are still ongoing, but these methods seem to provide some positive results.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">If a Lodge member falls unconscious due to suffocation or drowning, Father\u2019s Howl can extend its perception through the cultist and can take direct control of the comatose werewolf, its howl filling their lungs with cold air as it puppets them.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The motherlode the Lodge seeks is, of course, the actual site of Mother Wolf\u2019s death. The problem is that this is almost certainly buried somewhere in the Gauntlet, as far as the Cult can tell, although they\u2019re still unsure why this is the case; there must be a physical or spiritual location in the world that Wolf fell, but the echoes of the Sundering are carried most strongly through the Gauntlet rather than in the twin worlds it splits apart. Some Cultists attempt to enslave Beshilu with the intention of having them gnaw into the Gauntlet and uncover the gravesite itself.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cult ritemasters are prolific fetish creators. A number of Pure totems who have opposed the Cult in the past have disappeared, abducted and imprisoned into Gravedigger fetishes that have sometimes then even been used to buy influence with the oblivious Pure who the totems once lorded over.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Experiments continue with amalgamating Uratha and ancient god-fragments. These are largely conducted in deep temple-earthworks the Lodge maintains, far from the sight of other Pure who might deem such spiritual unions as blasphemous. A carnival of horrors slithers and capers through the vaults of the Cult.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gravediggers can give brief resuscitation to freshly dead bodies by pressing their mouths to those of the dead and howling their breath into the cold lungs of the slain. This inflicts the Exhausted Condition on the Gravedigger, but reanimates the carcass for one day; it will obey the Gravedigger\u2019s commands, but possesses some rudimentary, burned-out level of sentience from its life, and if left alone will act according to those instincts. The breath in their lungs allows these dead to speak; the Gravedigger who reanimated the corpse can speak through it with their own voice remotely, if they wish. </span></li> </ul><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#052D49\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tools </b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Cult of Bones has access to the Lodge Connections, Lodge Lorehouse and Lodge Stronghold merits. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bonesplinter Talisman (Fetish ooo) </b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Digging up the dead risks the wrath of restless shades, but the clattering bone fragments of this talisman ward the bearer and turn such malignancy into another revelation.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Effect: </i>The bearer gains a +2 bonus to resist or contest the Numina and Influences of ghosts; when targeted by such powers, the bearer also gains the clear impression of the ghost\u2019s name \u2013 if it had one \u2013 and the date and era of its death. </span></span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T15:17:51-07:00","id":1209026,"title":"","content":"This is Amazing Chris!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T15:19:22-07:00","id":1209027,"title":"","content":"Very nice. If you're saving the really good material for Shunned By The Moon, the supplement will be excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T15:36:29-07:00","id":1209035,"title":"","content":"I feel like a broken record everytime you post something Chris. This is awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T16:05:27-07:00","id":1209038,"title":"","content":"So this is not the best you have in mind? Damn. <br /> <br /> Anyways, nice to be reminded of how the Pure are religious zealots foremost, not just a bunch of angry barbarians or deluded cat\u2019s paws.<br /> <br /> ... Hey wait, wasn\u2019t there a Maeljin related to Wolf\u2019s death as well? The one of Violence (can\u2019t remember its name)? The one who built its palace over Wolf\u2019s death site or something? I wonder how the Cult will react if they learn of that one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-19-2018, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T21:41:45-07:00","id":1209117,"title":"","content":"Great stuff, Chris!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209038#post1209038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Hey wait, wasn\u2019t there a Maeljin related to Wolf\u2019s death as well? The one of Violence (can\u2019t remember its name)? The one who built its palace over Wolf\u2019s death site or something? I wonder how the Cult will react if they learn of that one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is Viruhk-Ur, Souless Wolf. There is a rumor he can be once 'body' or just once ephemeral flesh of Mother Wolf. And there is even <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360414-souless-wolf-as-urfarah-remains\">whole topic about this interpretation</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T22:40:03-07:00","id":1209121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209038#post1209038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Hey wait, wasn\u2019t there a Maeljin related to Wolf\u2019s death as well? The one of Violence (can\u2019t remember its name)? The one who built its palace over Wolf\u2019s death site or something? I wonder how the Cult will react if they learn of that one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite involved as much as 'glutted himself with it.' Thurifuge, the Architect of Violence who 'feeds on the spiritual resonance of every act of violence that has occurred since the dawn of time, and many Ithaeur with a twisted interest in the Maeljin have said that Thurifuge stands on the cusp of becoming a Celestine' that being Luna and Helios' Rank. Apparently he was relatively weak before, but the act of treachery of Father Wolf's killing bumped him up to Incarna, Rank 5-7. And, as you remembered, supposedly celebrated the promotion by building his palace out of Father Wolf's remains, on the spot where he died.<br /> <br /> While I always wanted more information about the Maeljin, the majority of information about them being in two books has helped. The above information was from Lore of the Forsaken, which has a section on each of the Maeljin. The other is, of course, Blasphemies. I'm looking forward to seeing what becomes of the Maeljin in second edition, but if the story sticks across editions it's still possible over the millennia some of the 'bricks' have been stolen or traded away, scattered across the cosmos. Given the legends of the place it would be a great bargaining chip Thurifuge could hold over the Uratha. Even if the place was a solid Father Wolf fossil it would still be a great undertaking to wrest it away from such a powerful entity and the cult is probably right to hedge their bets by making sure its grand resurrection (if possible) comes without any weakness if it's going to have to face off against the Architect of Violence at the moment of its rebirth.<br /> <br /> Really cool lodge. It's nice to have one with a link to ancestor spirits, something I was trying to work into the game I'm running now. I like that they're Pure but not quite in line with the rest of the Pure while definitively not being Forsaken-sympathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T23:46:42-07:00","id":1209129,"title":"","content":"Well, that was terrifying :P While my reaction for the original Cult of Bones was kinda &quot;meh&quot;, I do really dig (not pun intended) this presentation. I must say that while reading this, all I could ever think about was &quot;oh, holy simplicity!&quot;. I mean, let's say they would awaken Father Wolf from the dead. They have no idea that the chances are he would kill them all first, considering that they have ripped away their Auspices and that his last memory is <i>being killed by his own children</i>. And after unleashing that ancient terror upon the world, how long it would take the Forsaken to understand they are going to need to kill their maker <i>again</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:16:24-07:00","id":1209133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209129#post1209129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And after unleashing that ancient terror upon the world, how long it would take the Forsaken to understand they are going to need to kill their maker <i>again</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the world would change drastically enough that they'd have other problems to deal with. But there's no reason to think they would need to kill him. It was right to do at the time, the Forsaken believe, but no reason to do it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:22:39-07:00","id":1209134,"title":"","content":"Well, Father Wolf was a terrifying thing to behold back when he was alive- I highly doubt that dying has made him kinder. I could easily see Uratha, both Forsaken and Pure, who decide that perhaps having the Great Predator revived was not the best idea, and that in order to stop the world from turning into Hunter's Paradise/Living Hell for everyone else, they may need to put him down again.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but &quot;dead gods being revived&quot; is never a good thing in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:33:19-07:00","id":1209135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209134#post1209134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Father Wolf was a terrifying thing to behold back when he was alive- I highly doubt that dying has made him kinder. I could easily see Uratha, both Forsaken and Pure, who decide that perhaps having the Great Predator revived was not the best idea, and that in order to stop the world from turning into Hunter's Paradise/Living Hell for everyone else, they may need to put him down again.<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but &quot;dead gods being revived&quot; is never a good thing in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I fully appreciate that this would effectively 'wreck' the world as we know it, the Forsaken as a whole have an opportunity here that was, before, out of reach. Father Wolf was legended as the creator of Pangaea. A place where the Uratha belong. Choosing between having that back or ensuring the rest of the world faces the endless chaos and darkness and damning themselves all over again, you'd have plenty of Uratha, and probably even tribal totems, the Firstborn and Luna herself going for the former.<br /> <br /> If he brought back the Border Marches, he'd win over most Uratha. Him being scary doesn't mean he's not Father Wolf. Becoming more like him is one of the reasons werewolves delve into their Primal Urge. It's why the Storm Lords go through Abni-Gur, to be a new Father Wolf. It's why they literally carry on his duty, thousands of years on, with the tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2018, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:48:22-07:00","id":1209136,"title":"","content":"I don't know- I personally think he would be quit resentful and far from as powerful when he died, not to mention at his peak- sure, still powerful enough to change the world, but still greatly weakened. Again, that's entirely depends on how you view the Great Predator and your own personal interpertation, but the way I see it dying would greatly alter the Great Predator's personality. Would he start slaughtering Uratha for their Essence? Would she attack her own Firstborn for what she sees as betrayal? Would the Storm Lords feel betrayed for having their fate &quot;denied&quot; from them by Urfarah's return? Would the Iron Masters be split over deciding if they should celebrate the change of the world, or mourn for it falling back to the past? <br /> <br /> Sure, it depends entirely on how you play it and your needs for the game- but I just can't imagine a scenario which goes like &quot;Father Wolf is back, Pangaea is back, all the Uratha are happy again&quot;. Those are the Chronicles of Darkness. Things are never that simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:00:19-07:00","id":1209140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209136#post1209136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know- I personally think he would be quit resentful and far from as powerful when he died, not to mention at his peak- sure, still powerful enough to change the world, but still greatly weakened. Again, that's entirely depends on how you view the Great Predator and your own personal interpertation, but the way I see it dying would greatly alter the Great Predator's personality. Would he start slaughtering Uratha for their Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically what this lodge deals with. 'If Mother Wolf was weakened before its death, then the Cult must restore that strength, and so they hunt for those spirits with the closest resonance to the Great Predator.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would she attack her own Firstborn for what she sees as betrayal? Would the Storm Lords feel betrayed for having their fate &quot;denied&quot; from them by Urfarah's return? Would the Iron Masters be split over deciding if they should celebrate the change of the world, or mourn for it falling back to the past? </div> </div> </div>That's story. No way to know though Storm Lords feeling betrayed seems unlikely, they can still get close.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, it depends entirely on how you play it and your needs for the game- but I just can't imagine a scenario which goes like &quot;Father Wolf is back, Pangaea is back, all the Uratha are happy again&quot;. Those are the Chronicles of Darkness. Things are never that simple. </div> </div> </div>You know very well I didn't say all that 'all the Uratha are happy again.' You said that the Forsaken would try and kill him again, I thought that was nonsense. Of course things wouldn't just have a happy ending. The Pure would go crazy over finding out the truth about the brands, some tribes would fall apart, world politics would go bonkers as suddenly borders are useless. But the Forsaken would not be Forsaken anymore. That name is what they were called by the Pure for killing Father Wolf and losing Pangaea. It would be a colossal win for them, fraught with new perils, but still a great win. Comparable to vampires getting over the bane of sunlight and mages getting rid of the Curse of Quiescience or having everyone become Sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2018, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:04:22-07:00","id":1209141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209129#post1209129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that was terrifying :P While my reaction for the original Cult of Bones was kinda &quot;meh&quot;, I do really dig (not pun intended) this presentation. I must say that while reading this, all I could ever think about was &quot;oh, holy simplicity!&quot;. I mean, let's say they would awaken Father Wolf from the dead. They have no idea that the chances are he would kill them all first, considering that they have ripped away their Auspices and that his last memory is <i>being killed by his own children</i>. And after unleashing that ancient terror upon the world, how long it would take the Forsaken to understand they are going to need to kill their maker <i>again</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, Uratha would still be it's bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T01:52:58-07:00","id":1209151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209140#post1209140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's basically what this lodge deals with. 'If Mother Wolf was weakened before its death, then the Cult must restore that strength, and so they hunt for those spirits with the closest resonance to the Great Predator.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it depends on the level of success of the Lodge. I believe that at best the Lodge would get Father Wolf to the level he had when he died, and even that's its not likely. You may rule otherwise, but that's the way I see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's story. No way to know though Storm Lords feeling betrayed seems unlikely, they can still get close. </div> </div> </div>I didn't meant to say that the tribe as whole would feel betrayed. Hence the question mark at the end of the line. I've talked about the possibility that at least some packs and lodges, especially those who aim to become the new Father Wolf, would feel. I'm sorry if it wasn't clear, but I didn't want to derail the thread too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>You know very well I didn't say all that 'all the Uratha are happy again</b>. </div> </div> </div>It seems I have offended you. I'm sorry if that was the case. I have not meant to do so. Actually, I <i>did</i> understood you that you have said that it was more or less of an &quot;happy ending&quot;, and I did understood you acknowledged the chaos which would awaken from the revival. Just to note, in my book, getting rid of the bane of sunlight for vampires and removing the Lie for mages would also have bad side effects, which would cause certain negative side effects which I prefer to not detail in here in order to not derail the thread. The way I see it, enough werewolves, both Pure and Forsaken, would have enough motivations to act against Father Wolf's rebirth, as the Uratha are people, and not all of them would react the same way for the return of their progenitor. Even not all of the Firstborn would react in the same way, not to mention the spirit ecology as whole, as spirits are &quot;people&quot; too.<br /> <br /> It is seems you have your own vision for the state in which Father Wolf would be revived and its direct and indirect consequences. I apparently have my own. No need to be offended, and if you would like to continue the discussion I suggest we'll start a new thread for it, in order to not spam this beautiful one with internet spite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:55:36-07:00","id":1209246,"title":"","content":"I feel like Storm Lords in general and Gamir in particularly would jump at the chance of literally cannibalizing Wolf all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T08:27:57-07:00","id":1209266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209014-anshega-april-cult-of-bones-2e?p=1209151#post1209151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No need to be offended, and if you would like to continue the discussion I suggest we'll start a new thread for it, in order to not spam this beautiful one with internet spite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely not necessary, though I don't think my disagreeing with you was any reason for offense, you clearly have your own ideas about how the setting works. I made my point in my posts and offered reasons why the resurrection of their progenitor-god would be seen as a good thing and not the reason for a new, global sacred hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:01:03-07:00","id":1209299,"title":"","content":"False Father: Yes, I know exactly where your Father's bones lie. I would be happy to tell you, but what I need in return is a hug. Surely it's not that much to ask?<br /> False Father: Yeeesss... hug daddy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:58:25-07:00","id":1209818,"title":"","content":"I've always liked the Cult of Bones, so this is pretty cool to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-20T19:55:11-07:00","id":1261875,"title":"","content":"Sorry, should not have necro'd this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}